        "name": "Edwin",
        "username": "Edwin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-01T08:36:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\"Whenever O-X is dealt damage of a type reduced by a Plating card\"...does that mean the damage actually <em>has</em> to be reduced, or just that it happens to be of the type that your current Plating reduces?&nbsp; In other words, if the damage is irreducible, can it trigger RPS if it's the right type, or does being irreducible automatically prevent RPS from applying?&nbsp; (I played it on the assumption it was the latter, and we still won, so I figure I made the right call.&nbsp; Though it sure was close.)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:37.830Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
