        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>&quot;Whenever O-X is dealt damage of a type reduced by a Plating card&quot;...does that mean the damage actually <em>has</em> to be reduced, or just that it happens to be of the type that your current Plating reduces?&nbsp; In other words, if the damage is irreducible, can it trigger RPS if it&#39;s the right type, or does being irreducible automatically prevent RPS from applying?&nbsp; (I played it on the assumption it was the latter, and we still won, so I figure I made the right call.&nbsp; Though it sure was close.)</p>",
